# port-patches.sh: keep-p0 @ 820d104ac9ac over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits 863b5f903e44..2cb4f1d2ccf8); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
glm_cuda: prompts fill a 2048-row chunk a step between decode rounds behind TF_GLM_FILL=1 (concurrent fills, step A)

A prompt pass ran whole on the lane thread, so every decoding stream waited
for all of it (an 18.7 s decoder gap behind a 38k-token cold prefill on the
pair). With TF_GLM_FILL=1 the lanes take the core's sliced fills
(prefill_begin / fill_step) and a step runs one prompt chunk; off (the
default) nothing changes.

- cuda_prefill_loop: Plan (the pass's runs as prefillWith cut them: the keep
  point, the 64-token grid point below the end, the head's run), Cursor (a
  chunk at a time with run's own checkJob step) and chunkAt (run's loop
  body; run is checkJob plus a loop of it).
- cuda_engine: prefillWith is a Fill run to its end (startPass, then
  passChunk until done), so a sliced fill runs the same chunks, keep and
  draw as the whole pass; fillBegin / fillStep / fillFree run it a chunk a
  step, each chunk binding the fill's own sequence to the prompt path first
  (cache view, conv, rec, pos_dev, parity, the drafters' prompt position).
  startPass enters the MTP head one row behind at the pass's begin and the
  fill's prompt position starts there (the MTP-cache patch's rules, kept
  across steps); the digest is logged at the prompt's end. MTP drafts
  (FillWithMtp: one head for every stream) and media (FillWithMedia) are
  refused at fillBegin; the lanes never ask for either.
- cuda_lanes: the sliced path follows pass(): the resume is restored at the
  begin and no kept state is held across steps (after a mark the next
  segment goes on from the live rows); the room and the save's outcome are
  agreed at each mark; each segment ends with its note to rank 1; a step
  advances one chunk in all, the oldest fill's; structured output's bits are
  kept for the last draw; a prompt with pictures runs whole at its begin;
  sliced fills borrow no twin (the history is fetched); the first token's
  handle is the lane's own.
- cuda_mirror: the Leader sends the first token's bits with prefill_begin
  and arms a prefill's deadline for a prompt with media.
- cuda_native / cuda_serving: TF_GLM_FILL (1, or 0/unset), in the ranks'
  settings text only when on, refused with MTP drafts after the agreement;
  Serving.init sets it before the mirror takes the vtable.

Switches: TF_GLM_FILL (0; 1 on, refused with DRAFTER=mtp). Off: the vtable
is the old one, and prefillWith runs the same launches in the same order.

Tests: the plan against the old prefillWith's run calls; sliced against
whole on two ranks (first token, passes, kept marks, notes), one chunk a
step oldest first, a cancel mid-fill, keep floor and refused saves, a save
refused on rank 1 only, the mask, pictures, KV shard without twins, decode
rounds between a long fill's steps (lanes core and lane host); a fill
refused for memory is requeued; no long pass is held for restores under
slices. With the patches before it: the MTP head through a Fill's plan
(cache off, a keep point, the lanes' mark segments, resumes from each kept
state), fillBegin's refusals before anything moves, and the 1M coverage
sweep's chunk model checked against the Plan's cut (with and without a keep
point). Seven of the lanes tests failed on the old sliced code first.

Measured on the pair: not run yet (the next session: exact with it off and
on, the decoder gap during a 38k cold prefill, KV shard with fills, the MTP
refusal at start).

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo).
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0026-zig-glm-fill-steps.patch

